BT /F1 11 Tf 54 760 Td 15 TL (CINESCOPE — two-page write-up source) Tj T* (Problem and motivation) Tj T* (Movie reviews contain useful but noisy language about audience sentiment.) Tj T* (CINESCOPE studies binary document-level sentiment classification and turns the) Tj T* (result into an explainable demo for a live evaluation.) Tj T* (Dataset) Tj T* (We use the official IMDb Large Movie Review Dataset: 25,000 labeled training) Tj T* (reviews and 25,000 labeled test reviews, balanced across positive and negative) Tj T* (classes. The paper describes deriving labels from rating thresholds, but the) Tj T* (public benchmark does not expose each original rating; therefore our work is a) Tj T* (reproducible reproduction attempt rather than an exact replication.) Tj T* (Approach and implementation) Tj T* (Text is lowercased, tokenized, stripped of punctuation, numbers, and common) Tj T* (stopwords, and represented by normalized TF-IDF unigrams and bigrams. A deterministic) Tj T* (sparse logistic regression optimizer trains on the official training split.) Tj T* (The vectorizer and model are persisted together. The API returns a class,) Tj T* (positive probability, and weighted feature contributions. The static frontend) Tj T* (is responsive and intentionally black-and-white to keep the experiment and) Tj T* (explanation prominent.) Tj T* (Evaluation and conclusions) Tj T* (The evaluation command computes accuracy, precision, recall, F1, and confusion) Tj T* (counts on the untouched test split. Full results are generated by the command) Tj T* (rather than invented in documentation. The design makes split handling and) Tj T* (preprocessing auditable, while the model's feature weights make a prediction) Tj T* (inspectable. Future work should reproduce the paper's binary/count/n-gram) Tj T* (comparisons and six model families in an environment with scikit-learn, then) Tj T* (report runtime and statistical variability.) Tj T* (`python3 -m cinescope.cli download`, `train`, `evaluate`, and `serve` provide) Tj T* (the complete path. Unit and API tests use fixtures, do not require a network,) Tj T* (and verify preprocessing, persistence, metrics, inference, and validation.) Tj T* ET
